<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine monthly grain/oilseed shipments.</title>
<headline>Argentine monthly grain/oilseed shipments.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agriculture Secretariat</p>
<p>August grain shipment figures (tonnes), followed by</p>
<p>January-August totals (year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> Wheat	123,337  (210,174)     3,039,611  (5,917,648)</p>
<p> Maize    1,057,665  (388,347)     5,936,303  (5,198,347)</p>
<p> Sorghum     56,488   (14,850)	 634,614    (147,862)</p>
<p> Barley	   nil	(nil)	   6,888     (21,400)</p>
<p> Soybeans   239,471  (242,780)     1,969,150  (2,561,418)</p>
<p> Sunseed	  330   (16,264)	 536,447    (809,488)</p>
<p> Others	41,102   (18,639)	 201,280    (171,177)</p>
<p>Principal destinations in August were as follows (tonnes):</p>
<p>WHEAT: Brazil 121,451; Uruguay 1,738; Netherlands 148</p>
<p>MAIZE: Egypt 173,802; Japan 103,668; South Korea 88,013;</p>
<p>Malaysia 80,618; Taiwan 66,559; Venezuela 64,682</p>
<p>--Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655</p>
</text>
